{"title":"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the radius of a circle inscribed in a rhombus with diagonals of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcdffc2f42c00981ec586cc781534a4f000d36ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }4 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }\\frac {58}{13} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }\\frac{60}{13} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }5 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ }6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"368\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916304c9c9c4632f82f2a0cac6d82ff782486840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e943b6c4df768bd6a16459410c985eb16985d1b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_2=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> be the lengths of the diagonals, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> the side, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> the radius of the inscribed circle.\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> we can compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/624df5fa5379a4aca11a674c423e244dded68666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\sqrt{ (d_1/2)^2 + (d_2/2)^2 }=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"229\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>We can now express the area of the rhombus in two different ways: as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/6/216772b764793f5d6c940f03ad4c113a292373a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1 d_2 / 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, and as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47995fa4d664998d3abdb921140bac64aac525b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ar$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f2827ab3ab4df6a80ff84bf25a556e2dddae09e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1 d_2 / 2 = 2ar$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b95bdab01f9a301aa4c8c7a53e75f2ebde88cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\boxed{\\frac{60}{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"66\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>(The first formula computes the area as one half of the circumscribed rectangle whose sides are parallel to the diagonals. The second one comes from the fact that we can divide the rhombus into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equal triangles, and in those the height on the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. See pictures below.)\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/2303c6252536624af6d17519867812d65c95e642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); pair A=(-3,0), B=(0,-1.25), C=(3,0), D=(0,1.25); pair E=(-3,-1.25), F=(-3,1.25), G=(3,1.25), H=(3,-1.25); fill ( E -- F -- G -- H -- cycle, lightgray ); draw ( E -- F -- G -- H -- cycle ); draw ( A -- B -- C -- D -- cycle ); label(&quot;$d_1$&quot;,(E+F)*0.5,W); label(&quot;$d_2$&quot;,(F+G)*0.5,N); [/asy]\" width=\"312\" height=\"145\" /></center>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39997feae4fb3b6d4af1ebe941e93a0483f720e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); pair A=(-3,0), B=(0,-1.25), C=(3,0), D=(0,1.25); pair P = intersectionpoint( A--B--C--D--cycle, circle( (0,0), 15/13 ) ); fill ( A -- B -- (0,0) -- cycle, lightgray ); draw ( A -- B -- (0,0) -- cycle ); draw ( A -- B -- C -- D -- cycle ); draw ( circle( (0,0), 15/13 ) ); draw ( (0,0) -- P ); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(A+B)*0.5,SW); label(&quot;$r$&quot;,P*0.5,0.5*NW); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"122\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME\" title=\"1999 AHSME\">1999 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b